(5174696, 750097, 58247, '<td valign="top">I like this. How you got the model to swim with Koi I''ll never know! ;-)<br/> <br/>*Revisited*<br/> <br/>Well now I know how you got her to swim with the Koi! I think this is a good complement to your image in the other challenge. (No change in my scoring of this image)</td>', 'I like this. How you got the model to swim with Koi I''ll never know! ;-) *Revisited* Well now I know how you got her to swim with the Koi! I think this is a good complement to your image in the other challenge. (No change in my scoring of this image)', '2009-01-06 12:18:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5174698, 750008, 58247, '<td valign="top">Clever idea. Good Job!</td>', 'Clever idea. Good Job!', '2009-01-06 12:18:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5174726, 751593, 58247, '<td valign="top">Technically speaking this image is well done. The lighting, exposure, and lining up of the image is spot on. However, personally  don''t like how this image is a blatant rip off of a previous Transparency Challenge''s ribbon winning image. I''m all for seeing a cool shot on DPC and then going and trying to recreate the image yourself to see if you can do it. I''ve done that plenty of times. It''s a great way to try and improve your own shooting by attempting to duplicate a cool shot that inspired you here on DPC. But to then enter that same concept or idea in another version of the same challenge just strikes a bad cord with me. <br/> <br/>Please don''t take this as some kind of personal attack. It is not. It''s just how I feel. Despite my personal feelings, I still scored this image above average.</td>', 'Technically speaking this image is well done. The lighting, exposure, and lining up of the image is spot on. However, personally  don''t like how this image is a blatant rip off of a previous Transparency Challenge''s ribbon winning image. I''m all for seeing a cool shot on DPC and then going and trying to recreate the image yourself to see if you can do it. I''ve done that plenty of times. It''s a great way to try and improve your own shooting by attempting to duplicate a cool shot that inspired you here on DPC. But to then enter that same concept or idea in another version of the same challenge just strikes a bad cord with me.  Please don''t take this as some kind of personal attack. It is not. It''s just how I feel. Despite my personal feelings, I still scored this image above average.', '2009-01-06 12:30:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5174782, 750968, 32345, '<td valign="top">Probably the best looking image in this challenge, but I think it''s out of the box a little bit too much. Still... I''m back to raise my score to 9<br/> <br/>Well done</td>', 'Probably the best looking image in this challenge, but I think it''s out of the box a little bit too much. Still... I''m back to raise my score to 9 Well done', '2009-01-06 12:46:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5174877, 751458, 87410, '<td valign="top">Looks as clean as an IreneM photo...could it be?</td>', 'Looks as clean as an IreneM photo...could it be?', '2009-01-06 13:11:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175019, 751153, 101668, '<td valign="top">Real colourful and interesting.</td>', 'Real colourful and interesting.', '2009-01-06 14:23:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175043, 751155, 101668, '<td valign="top">Brilliant picture</td>', 'Brilliant picture', '2009-01-06 14:41:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175061, 750094, 101668, '<td valign="top">Great picture this one. Certainly one of the best</td>', 'Great picture this one. Certainly one of the best', '2009-01-06 14:53:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175072, 751155, 58247, '<td valign="top">The technique here is well executed.  However I will say to you (as I did on another image in this challenge) that I personally don''t like how this image is a blatant rip off of a previous Transparency Challenge''s ribbon winning image. I''m all for seeing a cool shot on DPC and then going and trying to recreate the image yourself to see if you can do it. I''ve done that plenty of times. It''s a great way to try and improve your own shooting by attempting to duplicate a cool shot that inspired you here on DPC. To be fair, this concept has been done many times here on DPC. But the fact that this idea was a ribbon winning entry for a previous Transparency Challenge tells me that you just took what worked before and emulated it hoping to score well too and that strikes a bad cord with me.<br/> <br/>Please don''t take this as some kind of personal attack. It is not. It''s just how I feel. Despite my personal feelings, I still scored this image above average.</td>', 'The technique here is well executed.  However I will say to you (as I did on another image in this challenge) that I personally don''t like how this image is a blatant rip off of a previous Transparency Challenge''s ribbon winning image. I''m all for seeing a cool shot on DPC and then going and trying to recreate the image yourself to see if you can do it. I''ve done that plenty of times. It''s a great way to try and improve your own shooting by attempting to duplicate a cool shot that inspired you here on DPC. To be fair, this concept has been done many times here on DPC. But the fact that this idea was a ribbon winning entry for a previous Transparency Challenge tells me that you just took what worked before and emulated it hoping to score well too and that strikes a bad cord with me. Please don''t take this as some kind of personal attack. It is not. It''s just how I feel. Despite my personal feelings, I still scored this image above average.', '2009-01-06 15:00:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175125, 751303, 101590, '<td valign="top">Well done: I like the colours, the composition and the way the city is "bokeh"ed completely, inlcuding the milky reflection in the water.. 10</td>', 'Well done: I like the colours, the composition and the way the city is "bokeh"ed completely, inlcuding the milky reflection in the water.. 10', '2009-01-06 15:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
