(5177350, 751606, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yospiff:</b></div><hr/><i> Very grainy, very soft. I''m not sure if that was an intentional creative choice on your part or not. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Nope. Just came out that way!</td>', 'Originally posted by yospiff: Very grainy, very soft. I''m not sure if that was an intentional creative choice on your part or not.  Nope. Just came out that way!', '2009-01-07 08:47:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177364, 750097, 61818, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, grats!  Doubly so for being the only ribbon winner to actually meet the challenge.</td>', 'Nice shot, grats!  Doubly so for being the only ribbon winner to actually meet the challenge.', '2009-01-07 08:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177395, 751547, 52549, '<td valign="top">Truly beautiful, love the fragility and textures. Excellent work, Steve.</td>', 'Truly beautiful, love the fragility and textures. Excellent work, Steve.', '2009-01-07 09:07:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177460, 751384, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by IreneM:</b></div><hr/><i>OMG! A ribbon! I''m off work this week and just got up. I thought I might make top 10 but didn''t dream I''d win a ribbon. Thank you!</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yeah, congrats on your first ribbon it''s about time you won one. Now stop messing around with those petty 5th and 6th place finishes and pass me already so I have a target again! ;-P</td>', 'Originally posted by IreneM:OMG! A ribbon! I''m off work this week and just got up. I thought I might make top 10 but didn''t dream I''d win a ribbon. Thank you! Yeah, congrats on your first ribbon it''s about time you won one. Now stop messing around with those petty 5th and 6th place finishes and pass me already so I have a target again! ;-P', '2009-01-07 09:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177470, 750097, 17203, '<td valign="top">Awesome- shoulda taken the blue IMO. Congrats!</td>', 'Awesome- shoulda taken the blue IMO. Congrats!', '2009-01-07 09:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177475, 751384, 38248, '<td valign="top">Way to go Irene!  Another blue for the D50 and that wonderful 60mm.  I going to get one of those lenses.  Great photo, great capture.</td>', 'Way to go Irene!  Another blue for the D50 and that wonderful 60mm.  I going to get one of those lenses.  Great photo, great capture.', '2009-01-07 09:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177520, 750508, 60495, '<td valign="top">Very moving shot, deserved higher score but it nice to see it recognized as a well deserved <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a> award winner.</td>', 'Very moving shot, deserved higher score but it nice to see it recognized as a well deserved  posthumous award winner.', '2009-01-07 09:43:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177526, 750097, 60495, '<td valign="top">Excellent image!</td>', 'Excellent image!', '2009-01-07 09:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177536, 750097, 67579, '<td valign="top">sweet photo Claire you never cease to amaze me, grats on the ribbon!<br/>-dave</td>', 'sweet photo Claire you never cease to amaze me, grats on the ribbon!-dave', '2009-01-07 09:52:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177552, 751462, 3724, '<td valign="top">v 9, a <i>bubble wrap experiment</i> - enjoy this wonderful soft effect.</td>', 'v 9, a bubble wrap experiment - enjoy this wonderful soft effect.', '2009-01-07 09:58:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177590, 751384, 49954, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KarenNfld:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AlexSaberi:</b></div><hr/><i> amazing shot. cant believe the amount of scores below 5. jealousy!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Jealousy? Actually if you read the challenge description, this does not meet the challenge:<br/> <br/>Create a photo in which a transparent or semi-transparent object is <i><b>between</b></i> you and your <b><i>subject</i></b>. <br/> <br/>So while I do think this is a beautiful photo, those low scores are justified and have nothing to do with jealousy.<br/> <br/>Sorry, Irene, for ranting on your photo. Congrats on the blue, it''s a wonderful photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agree with you 100% Karen.  Great photo!  But DNMC clearly as the "subject" to anyone objectives is the water splash and the bottle is not between the viewer and the subject.<br/> <br/>But again, great photo and has been proven here time and again, meeting the challenge is not a requirement with most voters.  Sad but true.<br/> <br/>Irene, I always love your work!</td>', 'Originally posted by KarenNfld: Originally posted by AlexSaberi: amazing shot. cant believe the amount of scores below 5. jealousy!!   Jealousy? Actually if you read the challenge description, this does not meet the challenge: Create a photo in which a transparent or semi-transparent object is between you and your subject.  So while I do think this is a beautiful photo, those low scores are justified and have nothing to do with jealousy. Sorry, Irene, for ranting on your photo. Congrats on the blue, it''s a wonderful photo.   Agree with you 100% Karen.  Great photo!  But DNMC clearly as the "subject" to anyone objectives is the water splash and the bottle is not between the viewer and the subject. But again, great photo and has been proven here time and again, meeting the challenge is not a requirement with most voters.  Sad but true. Irene, I always love your work!', '2009-01-07 10:09:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177622, 751384, 52115, '<td valign="top">This is a typical "IreneM" watershot<br/>It seems the splash didn''t come from the bottle, is that correct?<br/>Please give some setup details.<br/> <br/>From May-Dec 2006 you got no ribbons, but in 2008 you hit the jackpot.<br/>So I guess <b>persistence pays off</b>.<br/> <br/>Great record, 16-1st + 11-2nd + 11-3rd = 38, (19-HMs)<br/>Scalvert''s record: 15-1st + 19-2nd + 12-3rd, = 46, (7-HMs)<br/>IF you count HMs, you beat Scalvert, 57 to 53.<br/> <br/>I''d say you <b>Animate the Inanimate</b>.<br/></td>', 'This is a typical "IreneM" watershotIt seems the splash didn''t come from the bottle, is that correct?Please give some setup details. From May-Dec 2006 you got no ribbons, but in 2008 you hit the jackpot.So I guess persistence pays off. Great record, 16-1st + 11-2nd + 11-3rd = 38, (19-HMs)Scalvert''s record: 15-1st + 19-2nd + 12-3rd, = 46, (7-HMs)IF you count HMs, you beat Scalvert, 57 to 53. I''d say you Animate the Inanimate.', '2009-01-07 10:21:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177645, 750097, 58728, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Claire!  This is such an awesome image.</td>', 'Congratulations Claire!  This is such an awesome image.', '2009-01-07 10:27:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177647, 751153, 50641, '<td valign="top">the blur gives this a great sense of motion and depth - very dreamy!</td>', 'the blur gives this a great sense of motion and depth - very dreamy!', '2009-01-07 10:28:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177651, 750409, 80458, '<td valign="top">cant believe this didnt ribbon, my fav of the entries.</td>', 'cant believe this didnt ribbon, my fav of the entries.', '2009-01-07 10:28:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177653, 751384, 46177, '<td valign="top">I love your shot Irene and I personally think it does meet the challenge. My take is the subject is the liquid and the description didn''t say the entire shot needed to be seen through something transparent and obviously a portion of the liquid is seen through the transparent bottle.  So I think you met the challenge perfectly for me not to mention its an amazing image not only beautiful but well executed.  I am glad there is a vote and the majority of voters loved it.  Maybe if the descripition said the transparent object needed to fill more than say 80% of your image I would agree that it didn''t meet the challenge but that isn''t what it said. Regardless I think you deserved your blue and congratulations.  Keep shooting what you enjoy and let the rest of us have the pleasure of viewing the shots you do so well.<br/>Sorry for rambling on, everyone is entitled to there opinion and thats mine and I think the blue speaks for itself.</td>', 'I love your shot Irene and I personally think it does meet the challenge. My take is the subject is the liquid and the description didn''t say the entire shot needed to be seen through something transparent and obviously a portion of the liquid is seen through the transparent bottle.  So I think you met the challenge perfectly for me not to mention its an amazing image not only beautiful but well executed.  I am glad there is a vote and the majority of voters loved it.  Maybe if the descripition said the transparent object needed to fill more than say 80% of your image I would agree that it didn''t meet the challenge but that isn''t what it said. Regardless I think you deserved your blue and congratulations.  Keep shooting what you enjoy and let the rest of us have the pleasure of viewing the shots you do so well.Sorry for rambling on, everyone is entitled to there opinion and thats mine and I think the blue speaks for itself.', '2009-01-07 10:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5177668, 751458, 59276, '<td valign="top">beautiful image. just love that color</td>', 'beautiful image. just love that color', '2009-01-07 10:33:29.000000', NULL, 0),
