(5179008, 750138, 88580, '<td valign="top">Obviously, I have grossly overestimated the average voter''s intelligence.<br/> <br/>It does not bother me if the "deeper" meaning was not widely understood.  I realize many people may not have read any of the forum threads regarding this particular rule.  Still, I think anyone who has actually bothered to <i>read</i> the rules would be able to "get it."  But, that''s neither here nor there.<br/> <br/>I thought most members of a photography website would have at least <i>seen</i> a picture frame at some point.<br/> <br/>There is <i>glass</i> in the frame.  <i>Glass</i> is transparent.  I took a picture of a picture through the <i>glass</i> in the picture frame.  Why is it so difficult to see how that fits the challenge description?  It is not shoehorned; it is not out-of-the-box; it is <i>blatantly</i> in-your-face.</td>', 'Obviously, I have grossly overestimated the average voter''s intelligence. It does not bother me if the "deeper" meaning was not widely understood.  I realize many people may not have read any of the forum threads regarding this particular rule.  Still, I think anyone who has actually bothered to read the rules would be able to "get it."  But, that''s neither here nor there. I thought most members of a photography website would have at least seen a picture frame at some point. There is glass in the frame.  Glass is transparent.  I took a picture of a picture through the glass in the picture frame.  Why is it so difficult to see how that fits the challenge description?  It is not shoehorned; it is not out-of-the-box; it is blatantly in-your-face.', '2009-01-07 20:57:31.000000', NULL, 0),
